.TH scan_tofrom_array 3 "Version 1.0" "December 2023" "lib/textcode"
.SH NAME
scan_tofrom_array \- Scan data from an array and store it into another array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/textcode.h>
.sp
.BI "size_t scan_tofrom_array(size_t (*func)(const char*, char*, size_t*), array* src, array* dest)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function .BR scan_tofrom_array () scans data from an array and stores it into another array. The function takes the following parameters:
.sp
1. A pointer to a scanning function that takes a source string, a destination buffer, and a pointer to the size of the destination buffer, and returns the number of bytes processed from the source string.
2. A pointer to the source array.
3. A pointer to the destination array.
.sp
The function returns the number of bytes processed from the source array.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes processed from the source array.
.SH EXAMPLES
No examples are provided for this function.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B array, str
